https://solodit.cyfrin.io/issues/m-04-us.audit_content:
When the
LensHub
contract has been paused by governance (
_state
set to
ProtocolState.Paused
), users should not be able unfollow profiles. This can be inferred as the
unfollow()
function has the
whenNotPaused
modifier:
LensHub.sol#L368-L371
----new code block----
 function unfollow(uint256 unfollowerProfileId, uint256[] calldata idsOfProfilesToUnfollow)
 external
 override
        whenNotPaused
----end of code block ----
However, in the
FollowNFT
contract, which is deployed for each profile that has followers, the
removeFollower()
and
burn()
functions do not check if the
LensHub
contract is paused:
FollowNFT.sol#L131-L138
----new code block----
 function removeFollower(uint256 followTokenId) external override {
 address followTokenOwner = ownerOf(followTokenId);
 if (followTokenOwner == msg.sender || isApprovedForAll(followTokenOwner, msg.sender)) {
            _unfollowIfHasFollower(followTokenId);
        } else {
            revert DoesNotHavePermissions();
        }
    }
----end of code block ----
FollowNFT.sol#L255-L258
----new code block----
 function burn(uint256 followTokenId) public override {
        _unfollowIfHasFollower(followTokenId);
        super.burn(followTokenId);
    }
----end of code block ----
As such, whenever the system has been paused by governance, users will still be able to unfollow profiles by wrapping their followNFT and then calling either
removeFollower()
or
burn()
.
Impact
Users are able to unfollow profiles when the system is paused, which they should not be able to do.
This could be problematic if governance ever needs to temporarily pause unfollow functionality (eg. for a future upgrade, or unfollowing functionality has a bug, etc...).
Proof of Concept
The Foundry test below demonstrates how users will still be able to unfollow profiles by calling
wrap()
and
removeFollower()
, even after the system has been paused by governance. It can be run with the following command:
----new code block----
forge test --match-test testCanUnfollowWhilePaused -vvv
----end of code block ----
----new code block----
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.13;

import 'test/base/BaseTest.t.sol';

contract Unfollow_POC is BaseTest {
 address targetProfileOwner;
 uint256 targetProfileId;
    FollowNFT targetFollowNFT;

